{# Contents - front matter.

   3.1 fixes the order of the sections and does not ask for a contents page;
   this is the client's addition (decision 156). It answers to no switch in
   5.7's `sections` block, because it is not one of the seven sections - it is
   the page that says where they are.

   The page numbers are real. render_document lays the document out, reads back
   the page each section's anchor landed on, and renders again with those
   numbers, so a row here and the manifest's `sections` range for the same
   section come from one measurement (4.4). On the measuring pass the numbers
   are not known yet and the column is empty; the rows are the same height
   either way, so filling them in does not move what they point at. #}
<section class="section contents" id="contents">

  <h2>Contents</h2>

  <p class="lede">
    Where each part of this report begins. The same page numbers appear in the
    run manifest beside the section they belong to.
  </p>

  <table class="contents-table">
    <tbody>
      {% for row in contents %}
        <tr>
          <th>{{ row.label }}</th>
          <td class="figure">{{ row.page | show("") }}</td>
        </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>

</section>
